panel-right.more:
From top to bottom:

- **M** — the memory register, 31 green lamps numbered 0–30, each with a switch below;
- **RI** — the instruction register (code and address of the instruction being executed), under the inscriptions CODUL 2, CODUL 1, ADRESA 2, ADRESA 1 (code 2, code 1, address 2, address 1);
- **R I** — the micro-instruction register (7 lamps) and **RA** — the address register;
- **RAI** — the instruction address register, with switches, then INSTRUCTIA 1/2 (instruction 1/2) and MEMORIE TAMBUR/FERITE (drum/ferrite memory);
- the ANULEAZA (clear) and INTRODUCE (enter) commands;
- bottom: MEMORIE (memory), IMPULSURI (pulses), what the machine does on overflow, the status lamps and CALCULEAZA (compute).

The inscriptions are redrawn letter by letter from the textures of the 3D model; the lamp colours follow the 2011 photograph. The inscriptions stay in Romanian, as on the real console.
